WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.930
In 2023, Nigeria's maternal mortality ratio
was 993 deaths per 100,000 live births.

2
00:00:08.980 --> 00:00:11.230
Japan's was 3.

3
00:00:11.280 --> 00:00:13.090
Health is uneven.

4
00:00:13.140 --> 00:00:15.890
But one change shows up worldwide.

5
00:00:15.940 --> 00:00:20.590
In 2000, non-communicable diseases,
such as cardiovascular disease,

6
00:00:20.640 --> 00:00:25.510
cancers and diabetes, caused 58
per cent of the world's deaths.

7
00:00:25.560 --> 00:00:29.230
By 2023, they caused 74 per cent.

8
00:00:29.280 --> 00:00:32.490
So is that good news, or bad news?

9
00:00:32.540 --> 00:00:36.190
In this mission, you'll measure
health with healthy life expectancy,

10
00:00:36.240 --> 00:00:40.390
infant and maternal mortality,
sanitation and doctors.

11
00:00:40.440 --> 00:00:43.870
Then you'll test Abdel Omran's
epidemiological transition,

12
00:00:43.920 --> 00:00:47.790
first set out in 1971,
against the evidence.

13
00:00:47.840 --> 00:00:52.450
Your mission: decide whether the rise of
non-communicable diseases is good news

14
00:00:52.500 --> 00:00:55.330
or bad news, and justify your answer.
